# Copy to .env and adjust. Every VITE_ variable is inlined into the JavaScript
# bundle at build time, so treat all of them as public — never put a secret,
# API key or password here. Anything genuinely secret belongs on the backend.

# Where the app looks for the API. Defaults to http://127.0.0.1:8000 when
# unset, which is what `uvicorn app.main:app --port 8000` serves locally.
# 127.0.0.1 rather than localhost on purpose — see the note in src/lib/api.ts.
# VITE_API_URL=https://disciplined-production.up.railway.app

# Error reporting. Blank or unset disables Sentry entirely — and because Vite
# inlines this at build time, the guard in lib/observability.ts becomes a
# constant and the whole SDK is tree-shaken out, so an unconfigured build
# ships zero Sentry bytes and makes zero network calls. That is how dev and
# CI run.
#
# IMPORTANT: it follows that this must be set when the bundle is BUILT, not
# when it is deployed. Setting it only in the runtime environment of the web
# host, or after `npm run build`, produces an app with no reporting in it at
# all. For the native builds, it has to be set before `npm run ios` /
# `npm run android`.
#
# A DSN is a public, write-only identifier — safe to ship in a client bundle.
# Create a project at https://sentry.io and copy its DSN here.
# VITE_SENTRY_DSN=

# The build stamps itself with the current commit automatically (see
# resolveRelease in vite.config.ts). Set this only to override that, e.g. in
# a CI build with no git directory.
# VITE_RELEASE=
